Done. All four deliverables are written, and the write set was respected (only `docs/install/README.md`, `docs/install/PIPD_AGENT_INSTALL_PROMPT.md`, `.github/workflows/public-plugin-verify.yml`, `README.md`; no commit/push/tag, no `dist/`, `skills/`, `src/`, `schemas/`, `tools/`, `tests/`, `packaging/` edits by me).

## What I delivered

**1. `docs/install/README.md`** (new) — the install SSOT: exactly two routes (**Web**, **Agent**), the Web fallback's `DOC_MOUNT_ONLY` ceiling spelled out (no CLI / no MCP / no repo write / no S4 acceptance), the *conditional* Directory route, the five-state table (`BUILD_PASS` ≠ `PORTAL_APPROVED` ≠ `PUBLISHED` ≠ `HOST_QUALIFIED` ≠ `S4_FULL_PASS`, each with required evidence + state today), then advanced/recovery (version pin incl. the open tag-vs-served-asset item, hashes, uninstall/rollback, how to report a failure). Grounded on the real CLI (`--mount-pack/--release-id/--release-commit/--out`), the tool's real refusal codes, `docs/RELEASE_TUPLE.json`, and the 8 skills / 6 files each / 48 files.

**2. `docs/install/PIPD_AGENT_INSTALL_PROMPT.md`** (new) — one Traditional-Chinese copy-paste prompt (English identifiers kept). It forces the host to: identify host/version/OS, resolve the project root, list same-name skills, declare shell/file/network permissions; then SHOW target paths, file count, diff vs existing config, pinned 40-hex commit / ZIP sha256, uninstall path; STOP for explicit approval; refuse global writes, refuse `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` edits, refuse tokens/MCP/commit/publish, refuse a nonexistent directory install; then verify **real discovery + 8/8 effective load + one positive and one negative trigger**, reporting `NOT_VERIFIED` when only files were copied; and report host/OS/version, pinned source, effective count, refusal cases, raw log paths — without claiming S4 acceptance or publication.

**3. `.github/workflows/public-plugin-verify.yml`** (new) — read-only: `permissions: contents: read`, `pull_request` limited to the upgrade paths + `workflow_dispatch`, all three actions SHA-pinned with `persist-credentials: false`, no `pull_request_target`/secrets/tag/publish; a step proving no `skills|src|schemas` write; `py_compile` on the three tools; a fail-closed stdlib-only proof; the two new modules; the full suite; and two fail-closed negative steps (A: green-first, mutate the pack document, require real `^FAIL:` and the identity motive, reject import/collection errors; B: the fallback builder must emit `REFUSED MANIFEST_DIGEST_MISMATCH` on drifted bytes).

**4. `README.md`** — added an `## Install` section (two route entries + SSOT pointer); licence/history/evidence and every other section untouched.

